# Every file in this project is text, and every file is authored with LF.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf` decides per machine: a clone on Windows gets CRLF
# in the sources while the tests read those same sources and compare the bytes
# they contain — the Windows programs and the plugin-parity check both build
# strings out of them. Normalising to LF keeps a clone byte-identical to what the
# suites were run against, on either platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Electron binary lives in node_modules and is never tracked; this is only
# here so a stray archive is treated as binary rather than converted.
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
